 "notes": [
  "A bullish engulfing on 1h gave 14,641 entries in 1,996 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were level with random entries, at 0%, inside a luck band of -0.06% to 0.05%. On 4h it gave 3,657 entries in 494 separate moves. They finished 0.03% behind random, still inside the band.",
  "The default trigger, either engulfing, enters about twice as often as the bullish pattern alone on 1h. Its 29,437 entries make only 423 separate moves, because overlapping entries on one pair count once. It finished 0.01% behind random on 1h and 0.02% ahead on 4h, both inside the band. On daily it gives 21 separate moves, under the 30 the test needs, so it was never judged.",
  "A short after a bearish engulfing on SOL 1h was the one coin-level result that beat random, at 0.09%. It rests on 22 entries on Nov 4–10, 2022, during the FTX collapse. Without them the result is chance. It shows at 50 candles only, not at 10 or 100. Read as a long, the same signal was fragile and worse than random, for the same reason.",
  "On daily, the bearish engulfing splits by regime. As a short it was 2.31% ahead of random in uptrends and 0.58% behind in downtrends. Both sit inside their luck bands, and the uptrend band reaches 2.72%. The pooled 0.72% describes neither regime. On 1h and 4h, every setting stayed inside its band in uptrends and in downtrends.",
  "For a long DCA bot on these pairs, a bullish engulfing start condition times entries no better than a random candle. The DCA orders and take profit do the work. You can leave the pattern out, or test it as a filter beside a trend or level condition and judge that combination in a backtest. A bearish engulfing short on SOL 1h rests on the Nov 4–10, 2022 signals, so it fails as soon as no crash like that one follows the signals."
 ],
